---
title: Chana masala
servings: 2
tags: [indian, vegetarian, weeknight]
cuisine: indian
source: Chana Masala by Leanne Brown, PBS Food, https://www.pbs.org/food/recipes/chana-masala
---

Mix the @ground coriander{1%tbsp}, @ground turmeric{1%tsp}, @cayenne{1/4%tsp},
@garam masala{1/2%tsp}, @smoked paprika{1%tsp}(optional) and @salt{1/2%tsp} in
a small bowl.

Melt the @ghee{1/2%tbsp}(or butter with a splash of olive oil) in a small
#saucepan{} over medium-low heat. Add the @cumin seeds{1%tsp} and stir
~{5%seconds}, until fragrant.

Add the @onion{1}(small, chopped) and cook ~{2%minutes} to ~{3%minutes}. Add
the @garlic{3%cloves}(finely chopped) and cook ~{2%minutes}, then the
@ginger{1%tsp}(grated) and @jalapeño{1/2}(finely chopped) for ~{1%minute}.

Stir in the spice mix, then the @tomato puree{1%cup}(canned). Cover and let it
cook down ~{5%minutes} to ~{10%minutes}.

When the tomato has thickened and the ghee begins to separate out, add the
@cooked chickpeas{2 1/2%cups}(drained) and @water{1/2%cup}. Bring to a boil,
then simmer ~{10%minutes}, mashing a few chickpeas against the pan to thicken
the sauce.

Top with @cilantro{}(chopped) and spoon over @plain yogurt{}(or raita). Serve
with rice or roti.

> Seed the jalapeño for less heat.
